  prose(<<~'CANONICAL_PROSE', origin: :published)
    ## Origins
    
    ☽'ofund' Guild rose from Nightfall Shelf's volcanic depths during the Great Thaw as fire-merchants — extractors and traders of fire-cores drawn from the berg's geothermal veins. At their height, the guild controlled trade through Wane☽ Oncea, a fortified trade-hub whose vaults were carved with precision and whose lower chambers remain sealed behind warning glyphs reading *do not open*, carved by a guild-master whose name the records do not preserve. Trade routes were mapped in captured flame and authenticated by bone-marked contracts. The guild also held Nightfall Shelf and Thrall☽ Vavmastius, a territorial footprint that briefly rivaled the Icebound Exchange's surface holdings.
    
    ## The Faction Wars and After
    
    The Faction Wars dismantled this. The Icebound Exchange, Aurora Stack's governing trade authority, seized Wane☽ Oncea. Threshold, the Aurora-aligned faction, took Aurora Berg. ☽'ofund' clawed back Nightfall Shelf and Thrall☽ Vavmastius, though The Midnight Claws — Nightfall Shelf's dominant syndicate — later acquired Thrall☽ Vavmastius through a brokered agreement whose terms are not in the archive. During the wars, the guild conducted supply interdiction against the Midnight Claws under Pactum∴ne emergency provisions. The records are incomplete. No formal denial-of-trade was registered with the Shadow Parliament, the Nightshelf's governing legislative body. This absence is either an oversight or a decision; I am inclined toward the latter.
    
    Guild trade manifests from this period record crystal shipments through Terrace Momiou, the Aurora Stack's primary trade terrace, exceeding documented Aurora Stack exports by a factor of three. The guild filed these figures. It never challenged the discrepancy. Neither did anyone else.
    
    ## Trade Operations
    
    The guild's primary trade remains fire-cores, graded by burn-duration:
    
    | Grade | Burn Duration | Status |
    |---|---|---|
    | Forge-grade | 60 days | Extraction reduced by one-third; mining depths increasingly unstable |
    | Extended-burn | 140 days | Limited stock; premium pricing |
    
    Before each Long Dark, the guild stockpiles aurora-crystals in Wane☽ Oncea's upper vault. Once darkness falls, the crystals cannot be recharged — the pre-dark inventory becomes a fixed survival equation. Secure storage is maintained at Scar☽ Lucamlinaecius, a deep-carved depot beneath ☽'scar Ramtatus~, where sanctification surcharges and mandatory witnessed retrieval apply to lower-vault holdings.
    
    The guild lost access to The Fissured Smelt~, its primary source of forge-grade ore, after Wake-Singer forces — orca shamans devoted to waking their dead god — breached the site through mineral-water channels, killing guild defenders and forcing the sealing of the upper galleries. The Midway Shelf trade corridor has been suspended due to ongoing orca-related security threats.
    
    Each Long Dark costs the guild tunnel-runners and depot staff to the Walking. Sealed vaults show inventory counts that change between tallies. The guild reconciles these discrepancies at its own discretion and does not explain them. I have no evidence that would allow me to explain them either.
    
    ## The Foedus∴vincu and Legal Standing
    
    The guild operates under the Foedus∴vincu, an orca pact whose specific terms I have not been able to verify independently. The Shadow Parliament has refused to acknowledge the Foedus∴vincu, calling it unauthorized. The guild's charter is under Parliamentary review, its last formal holdings forfeit after a counter-claim by The Cell, a declining Nightshelf authority. Every guild shipment now moves under a fractured seal that authenticates nothing, rendering their trade technically contraband by the Parliament's own codes. ☽'ofund' continues using its charter designations regardless.
    
    The guild holds co-stewardship of The Glow-Fissure, a corruption source point, under rotation with Weal' Clique~. This role is formally recognized in the Accord of Still Pools and Frost Zenith, a treaty between the Aureate merchant guilds and the ☽'shadow Covens' Order that obliges both signatories to share corruption-monitoring data from the Fissure.
    
    ## Notable Personnel and Operations
    
    **Lovumruius~ Domina**, a guild merchant, severed all connections to the guild's collaborative research with Light-Regent Xouhoulong of Aurora Stack after a catastrophic breach in sealed chambers beneath the Hearth Plaza, where guild researchers and Xouhoulong's aurora-readers had been experimenting with deep-ice pressure-magic. Lovumruius~ Domina is currently subject to a Shadow Parliament recovery warrant for unauthorized fire-core extraction and possession of the central shard of Dagger☽ Vaesacsorius~, the guild's fractured ceremonial seal-artifact.
    
    **Niaecum~**, a veteran trader, arranged the contraband routes the Midnight Claws required under the Foedus∴vincu and remained behind after the guild's withdrawal from the Hearth Plaza. At Junction Twelve, a Nightshelf trade-nexus, Niaecum~ shared a bone-marked cartography tablet of deep-tunnel routes with the Wake-Singer delegation — a unilateral act giving orca chanters access to passages no other faction had walked. The routes would be sung into permanent memory, beyond any faction's ability to retract. Niaecum~'s name was carved in old-script at the guild's Junction Twelve trade-stall, a registration that by Nightshelf convention cannot be unstruck.
    
    **☽'aeteraea**, a guild merchant whose coded ledgers remain officially undecoded, vanished into the deep tunnels after the cleansing at Wane☽ Oncea destroyed her networks. **☽'Netemia Glow-bringer** carried artifacts over which the guild asserts custodial authority — a practice extended to all affiliates who die in the field. The guild also held the Thrumed~ Shadow-glass, a Nightshelf relic of crystallized power, and built a shrine to contain it — not from reverence but from fear. Additional artifacts under guild custody include the ☽'micseleia' Dagger and the Directrix Mirror, both awaiting restoration.
    
    ## Present Condition
    
    The guild that survives into the Frozen Peace is smaller, more cautious, and divided between hardliners who seek to reclaim lost holdings and pragmatists who understand the arithmetic. Both attend the same meetings in rotating guild-halls. Members carry amulets of fire-core authentication that authenticate less than they once did. The internal joke — that ☽'ofund' stands for 'Only Losses Found' — persists because it is easier to repeat than to refute. What holds the guild together is not hope but refusal: to dissolve, to disappear, to become what the Aurora Stack always whispered they were. They survived the Faction Wars and the Clever Ice Age by being too small to matter and too useful to eliminate. They have learned to live in that margin.
  CANONICAL_PROSE
