  annotation "note_1771577494602_1", anchor: "The guild filed these figures. It never challenged the discrepancy. Neither did anyone else.", text: "A smuggling operation that submits accurate paperwork documenting its own smuggling, then waits politely for someone to notice, is not criminal enterprise. It is performance art. The manifests are still in the Terrace Momiou administrative strata. Filed in triplicate.", type: :commentary, display: :popout
  annotation "note_1771577494602_2", anchor: "an orca pact whose specific terms I have not been able to verify independently", text: "I want to be precise about what 'not been able to verify' means. The deep ice preserves treaty-impressions with thermal clarity — the Flipper Accord's three secret renegotiations survived intact, every draft. The Foedus∴vincu leaves no such impression. Not a degraded impression. Not a partial one. None. Either this pact was sealed somewhere the ice cannot reach — which limits us to open water or volcanic vents — or the guild has been citing a document that does not exist as legal justification for arrangements that would otherwise constitute treason. Both possibilities delight me.", type: :skepticism, display: :full
  annotation "note_1771577494602_3", anchor: "a unilateral act giving orca chanters access to passages no other faction had walked", text: "The routes shared at Junction Twelve almost certainly include the mineral-water channels through which the Wake-Singers later breached The Fissured Smelt~. The timeline fits within a single season. The guild lost its primary forge-grade ore source to an assault using passages the entry itself describes as unknown to any faction — passages Niaecum~ had just handed over in cartographic form, to be sung into permanent memory beyond retraction. That the guild frames the Fissured Smelt~ loss as an external catastrophe rather than a consequence of its own member's actions is institutional self-preservation so brazen it almost constitutes honesty.", type: :correction, display: :full
  annotation "note_1771577494602_4", anchor: "after a catastrophic breach in sealed chambers beneath the Hearth Plaza", text: "See my annotation on the Hearth Plaza. The sealed galleries contained deep-ice pressure research sited adjacent to a corruption source under Mandatum∴absconditu. Xouhoulong knew. Lovumruius~ Domina's severance reads less like horror and more like an exit from a project whose real purpose had become undeniable.", type: :commentary, display: :popout
